# Published on the `data` branch as a local safety net.
#
# That branch carries build artifacts only and does not track this repo's
# source or .gitignore, so a checkout of it had nothing stopping `git add .`
# from staging live credentials. This file does — but it is a second layer:
# the sync workflow's guard (scripts/guard-data-branch.mjs) is the first.
#
# Keep this list secret-only. Do NOT ignore directing/, postproduction/ or
# cloudinary-mapping.json — those are the artifacts this branch exists for.

.env
.env.*
*.env
node_modules/
docs/SCHEMA-FULL.local.md
.DS_Store
.npmrc
.netrc
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
